2. COMPONENTS NOT PRESENT IN THESE ARTEFACTS
===============================================================================

The following components appear in the Android artefacts of this SDK and are
listed here solely to record that they are NOT linked into, and NOT delivered
with, the iOS artefacts. No attribution is due in respect of them for these
artefacts.

  - com.squareup.okhttp3:okhttp        (Android HTTP engine only)
  - com.squareup.okio:okio             (reached through OkHttp)
  - org.slf4j:slf4j-api           (via kotlinx-coroutines-slf4j, MIT)
  - org.jetbrains:annotations          (JVM target only)

The following components are bundled in the Kotlin/Native distribution but
are NOT linked into these artefacts (verified 2026-09-04, see entry [4],
METHOD): mimalloc (not the default allocator on this Kotlin version),
libffi, libbacktrace (release builds use core symbolication), zlib,
BoringSSL and libcurl (the HTTP engine is NSURLSession).

The iOS HTTP engine is ktor-client-darwin, which uses Apple's NSURLSession.
System frameworks provided by Apple are dynamically linked at runtime, are not
redistributed by Sirdata, and are governed by the Apple Developer Program
License Agreement rather than by this NOTICE.


